Q: What would be the fastest and memory-efficient way to print in zig 0.16.0(master)? A: <p>So actually having a fixed buffer on stack is much faster and behaves the same way so by replacing</p>
<pre class="lang-rust prettyprint-override"><code>const allocator = Allocator.allocator();
const count = try std.fmt.count(fmt, args);
const buf = try allocator.alloc(u8, count);
defer allocator.free(buf);
</code></pre>
<p>with</p>
<pre class="lang-rust prettyprint-override"><code>var buf: [1024]u8 = undefined;
</code></pre>
<p>and passing buf as buf[0..buf.len]<br />
This code will run 20-40 us(microseconds) faster</p>

Q: &quot;Suspicious receiver type; this does not apply to the current receiver of type ApplicationExtension&quot; after upgrading to AGP 9 A: <p>I've found solution, in Gradle Plugin v9, there is no need to add following syntax in <code>build.gradle.kts</code> anymore.</p>
<p>Kotlin Plugin</p>
<pre><code>plugins {
    alias(libs.plugins.kotlin.android)
}
kotlin-android = { id = &quot;org.jetbrains.kotlin.android&quot;, version.ref = &quot;kotlin&quot; }
</code></pre>
<p>JVM Target</p>
<pre><code>kotlin {
    compilerOptions {
        jvmTarget.set(JvmTarget.JVM_17)
    }    
}
</code></pre>
<p>by removing these two, my project build successfully.</p>
